The key ingredient in this proof is our precise control of the image of the right inverse $Q_{\alpha,y}$ (specifically, that $\operatorname{im} Q_{\alpha,y}=\ker L_\alpha$).

Suppose $(\alpha_i,y_i,\kappa_i)\to(\alpha,y,\kappa)$ is a convergent net.\footnote{We could restrict to sequences rather than nets since $\mathbb C^d\times\mathbb R^{\dim\overline{\mathcal M}^d}\times K$ is first countable.  However, this would not make the argument any simpler.}  We will show that:
